262
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:22,000
does not want a clean slaughter. The

263
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:24,640
crowd wants a story with a hero standing

264
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:27,360
in it. You learn to give them exactly

265
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:29,680
that story. You begin to see that

266
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:32,480
survival here is not only strength. It

267
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:34,720
is also performance. It is knowing what

268
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:37,440
the mob hungers for and feeding it to

269
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:39,839
them. You think of your son sometimes

270
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:42,399
between the fights. He would be 5 years

271
00:11:39,839 --> 00:11:45,519
old now. You hope he never learns what

272
00:11:42,399 --> 00:11:48,560
his father became inside these walls.

273
00:11:45,519 --> 00:11:50,320
Level five, the favorite.

274
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:52,480
Something changes for you in your fourth

275
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:54,640
year. The crowd begins to chant a name

276
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:56,640
when you enter the sand. It is not the

277
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:58,959
name your mother gave you. The ludist

278
00:11:56,640 --> 00:12:01,360
gave you a stage name on your first day.

279
00:11:58,959 --> 00:12:03,839
It was chosen to sound fierce and proud

280
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:06,399
in Latin. Now that name is painted

281
00:12:03,839 --> 00:12:09,200
across the city walls. Boys scratch it

282
00:12:06,399 --> 00:12:11,120
into wet plaster on every street. Women

283
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:14,000
send messages to the school asking for

284
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:16,639
you by it. The Romans are very strange

285
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:19,519
about their gladiators. They despise you

286
00:12:16,639 --> 00:12:22,160
and they desire you at the same time.

287
00:12:19,519 --> 00:12:24,639
You are the lowest of the low. You are a

288
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:26,880
slave with no rights under their law.

289
00:12:24,639 --> 00:12:29,600
And yet senators want to be seen

290
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:31,360
standing beside you. Wealthy women pay

291
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:33,839
handsomely for a single night with a

292
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:36,959
champion. Your sweat is scraped from

293
00:12:33,839 --> 00:12:38,720
your skin and sold as a charm. Men rub

294
00:12:36,959 --> 00:12:41,680
it on themselves hoping to borrow your

295
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:44,880
strength. It is absurd, but you take

296
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:47,360
whatever it brings you. A favorite eats

297
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:49,760
far better food. A favorite is given a

298
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:51,519
cell of his own. A favorite is matched

299
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:54,560
against men the editor thinks he can

300
00:12:51,519 --> 00:12:57,680
beat. The lenista guards his prize very

301
00:12:54,560 --> 00:13:00,480
carefully. You are his bull now, his

302
00:12:57,680 --> 00:13:02,480
money walking on two legs. He parades

303
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:04,399
you at the banquetss of rich men. He

304
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:06,880
rents you out for private shows in their

305
00:13:04,399 --> 00:13:09,440
gardens. A senator invites you to his

306
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:12,000
villa. You dine among men who own

307
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:14,480
provinces. They touch your scars like

308
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:17,120
you are stone. They ask you to describe

309
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:19,680
your kills. You tell the stories because

310
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:22,240
it is expected. A woman watches you

311
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:26,000
across the room. She is the senator's

312
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:28,079
wife. She is bored and beautiful. You

313
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:31,600
understand what is being offered. You

314
00:13:28,079 --> 00:13:34,000
are a slave. You cannot refuse it. You

315
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:36,399
go back to your cell before dawn. You

316
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,760
feel less like a man. You feel more like

317
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:39,680
a prize.

318
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:43,920
You tell yourself the freedom is worth

319
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:46,560
this. You almost believe it. The coins

320
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:49,040
all flow to him. You see almost none of

321
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:51,760
them yourself. But you see something far

322
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:54,000
more important than coins. You see a

323
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:56,800
path that does not end face down in the

324
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:59,440
dirt. A gladiator who wins enough fights

325
00:13:56,800 --> 00:14:02,320
can be granted his freedom. You once

326
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:04,399
believed mere survival was impossible.

327
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:07,120
Now you let yourself begin to imagine

328
00:14:04,399 --> 00:14:10,399
more. You begin to count differently in

329
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:13,120
your head. Not fights survived, but

330
00:14:10,399 --> 00:14:15,600
fights remaining until the door opens.

331
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:18,160
Each victory is a single coin laid down

332
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:20,480
toward that door. You stop thinking of

333
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:23,760
your old village every day. The memory

334
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:25,680
has gone soft and pale at its edges. You

335
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:28,639
can no longer picture your wife's face

336
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:31,920
clearly. That quiet loss frightens you

337
00:14:28,639 --> 00:14:35,360
more than any opponent ever has. Level

338
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:37,839
six, the champion. By your sixth year,

339
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:39,600
you are a true champion. You have won a

340
00:14:37,839 --> 00:14:42,000
crown of victories that almost no man

341
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:44,320
reaches. You have fought men from every

342
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:46,480
corner of the empire. You fought a Gaul

343
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:48,480
armed with a net and a trident. You

344
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:50,720
fought a giant from Germania who nearly

345
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:52,320
cracked your skull. You fought a fellow

346
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:54,800
Thrian who had been your friend in the

347
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:57,279
Lutus. That fight you never speak about

348
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:59,839
to anyone. He yielded to you on the open

349
00:14:57,279 --> 00:15:02,480
sand. He raised his finger and he looked

350
00:14:59,839 --> 00:15:05,120
into your eyes. The crowd screamed for

351
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:07,519
his blood. You looked to the editor and

352
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:09,920
you begged him with your face. He gave

353
00:15:07,519 --> 00:15:12,480
the killing signal anyway. You carry

354
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:15,279
that one with you always. You carry all

355
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:17,760
of them, but that one sits heaviest. You

356
00:15:15,279 --> 00:15:19,839
are famous across the whole region now.

357
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:22,079
Your image is painted on oil lamps and

358
00:15:19,839 --> 00:15:24,399
drinking cups. Rich men commission

359
00:15:22,079 --> 00:15:26,160
mosaics of your greatest fights.

360
00:15:24,399 --> 00:15:28,560
Children in the streets play at being

361
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:30,639
you. You have killed more men than you

362
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:33,600
can count. You stopped counting them

363
00:15:30,639 --> 00:15:36,880
long ago. Your girlfriend is gone by

364
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:39,120
now. He fell two years ago. A younger

365
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:41,600
man took him. You were not allowed to

366
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:45,680
mourn. You fought your own match that

367
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:47,680
afternoon. You won it. You felt nothing

368
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:51,040
that night. You understood what you had

369
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:54,639
become. A man who loses a brother and

370
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:57,519
kills anyway. You drank alone. You did

371
00:15:54,639 --> 00:16:00,079
not sleep. You saw his crooked nose

372
00:15:57,519 --> 00:16:02,480
behind your eyes. You promised to earn

373
00:16:00,079 --> 00:16:05,839
the freedom for both of you. You meant

374
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:08,399
it. You still mean it now. The killing

375
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:10,399
is only a craft now. You feel almost

376
00:16:08,399 --> 00:16:12,800
nothing while you are doing it. The

377
00:16:10,399 --> 00:16:15,600
feeling always comes later in the dark

378
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:17,920
of your cell. In your dreams, a wooden

379
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:19,839
sword is pressed into your hand. You

380
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:23,440
wake reaching for a weapon that is not

381
00:16:19,839 --> 00:16:25,839
there. You are 30 years old. Most

382
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:28,560
gladiators never live to see this age.

383
00:16:25,839 --> 00:16:30,800
The sand takes them young and hungry.

384
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:34,000
You have lived through skill and luck

385
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:36,560
and cold hard will. You did the things

386
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:38,399
the other men would not do. You have

387
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:41,040
become exactly what they shaped you

388
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:43,680
into. You are the finest killer this

389
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:46,079
school has ever produced. And the better

390
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:48,959
you become, the nearer the door of

391
00:16:46,079 --> 00:16:51,360
freedom draws. The crowd adores a

392
00:16:48,959 --> 00:16:53,680
champion above all other things. But the

393
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:56,079
crowd loves it even more when a champion

394
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:59,360
is finally set free.

395
00:16:56,079 --> 00:17:00,880
Level seven, the Freedman. It happens at

396
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:02,959
a great festival in the heart of the

397
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:04,880
city. The games are sponsored by a

398
00:17:02,959 --> 00:17:06,400
powerful magistrate. He wants a

399
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:08,880
spectacle that the people will never

400
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:11,520
forget. He wants to free a beloved

401
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:13,839
champion before the entire crowd. You

402
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:16,000
are the man he chooses for it. You fight

403
00:17:13,839 --> 00:17:18,400
your match under the burning sun. You

404
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:21,199
win exactly as you have won so many

405
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:23,679
times before. Then the editor rises

406
00:17:21,199 --> 00:17:26,559
slowly from his seat. He holds up a

407
00:17:23,679 --> 00:17:29,200
plain wooden sword for all to see. It is

408
00:17:26,559 --> 00:17:32,480
called the rutus. A man who receives the

409
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:35,520
rutus becomes a rudiarius. He is a free

410
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:38,640
man from that moment forward. The crowd

411
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:40,320
erupts into a single enormous roar. They

412
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:43,039
are screaming the stage name they gave

413
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:45,679
you years ago. The wooden sword is

414
00:17:43,039 --> 00:17:47,600
placed into your scarred hands. You have

415
00:17:45,679 --> 00:17:50,000
held a wooden sword since your first day

416
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:52,799
in this place. That first sword was the

417
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:55,520
tool of your slavery. This one is the

418
00:17:52,799 --> 00:17:58,400
symbol of your freedom. You fall to your

419
00:17:55,520 --> 00:18:00,240
knees and you weep on the sand.

420
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:04,880
Thousands of strangers weep along with

421
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:07,200
you. You are 31 years old.

422
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:09,840
You walked into Capua a chained captive

423
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:13,039
12 years ago. You walk out of the arena

424
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:15,600
a free man. But freedom is far stranger

425
00:18:13,039 --> 00:18:18,320
than you ever imagined it. You have no

426
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:20,799
home left to return to. Your village was

427
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:22,960
burned to ash the day they took you.

428
00:18:20,799 --> 00:18:25,840
Your wife and your son are a memory you

429
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:28,559
can barely hold. You have no trade in

430
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:31,120
this entire world except killing. You

431
00:18:28,559 --> 00:18:33,919
have money now, gifts from admirers, and

432
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:36,559
a small share at last. You could vanish

433
00:18:33,919 --> 00:18:38,559
into the empire and begin a new life.

434
00:18:36,559 --> 00:18:41,520
Many freed gladiators choose exactly

435
00:18:38,559 --> 00:18:44,640
that. But many others come straight back

436
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:48,080
to the sand. That first night of freedom

437
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:50,480
is the loneliest of your life.

438
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:53,440
You sleep in a real bed. There are no

439
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:56,320
bars. There are no chains. There are no

440
00:18:53,440 --> 00:19:00,320
guards at the door. You lie awake for

441
00:18:56,320 --> 00:19:02,480
hours. You do not know how to be free.

442
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:06,240
You spent your whole adult life in a

443
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:10,640
cage. The cage told you who you were.

444
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:13,280
Now the cage is gone. So is the answer.

445
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:17,039
You think of your gall friend. He never

446
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:19,280
got this. You weep again. You weep

447
00:19:17,039 --> 00:19:21,280
quietly this time.

448
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:24,320
The strange truth is that the arena

449
00:19:21,280 --> 00:19:27,360
calls its son's home. You walk a city

450
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:29,919
that no longer owns you. You are free

451
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:33,039
with no people and a single brutal

452
00:19:29,919 --> 00:19:36,640
skill. For the first time in your life,

453
00:19:33,039 --> 00:19:39,360
the next choice is yours alone.

454
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:41,600
Level eight, the trainer. You do not

455
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:43,919
leave the lutus. You find that you

456
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:45,840
simply cannot leave it. The school is

457
00:19:43,919 --> 00:19:48,240
the only world that has ever made sense

458
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:50,720
to you. The Leninista offers you a place

459
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:53,840
at his side. He wants you to become a

460
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:56,000
doctor. A doctor is the man who trains

461
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:57,840
the new fighters. He is a freed

462
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,640
gladiator who teaches the craft of

463
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:02,880
survival. You remember your own doctor

464
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:06,480
from all those years ago. You remember

465
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:09,039
his wooden rod and his hard, tired eyes.

466
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:10,880
Now you are the one who carries the rod.

467
00:20:09,039 --> 00:20:13,520
You stand in the same yard where you

468
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:16,160
once bled. You watch the fresh captives

469
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:18,480
arrive in chains. They come exactly as

470
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:20,960
you once came. They are young and

471
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:22,480
frightened and far from their homes.

472
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:25,360
Some of them cannot speak a word of

473
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:28,159
Latin. Some left wives and sons in

474
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:30,400
villages that no longer exist. You see

475
00:20:28,159 --> 00:20:32,880
your own younger self in every one of

476
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:34,960
them. You teach them to grip the heavy

477
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:37,760
wooden sword. You teach them to strike

478
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:40,080
the post a thousand times a day. You

479
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:42,000
teach them to read a man's shoulders.

480
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:44,480
You teach them every trick that ever

481
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,720
kept you breathing. You are harder on

482
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:48,960
them than your doctor was. You tell

483
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:52,080
yourself it keeps them alive. Part of

484
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:54,720
that is true. Part of it is colder. You

485
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:57,200
do not examine that part. The gentle

486
00:20:54,720 --> 00:21:00,000
ones die first. You learned that long

487
00:20:57,200 --> 00:21:02,480
ago. So you give the new men no

488
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:04,559
gentleness. You watch them break in the

489
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:07,280
first weeks. You watch some of them

490
00:21:04,559 --> 00:21:10,400
harden. You see the door close behind

491
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:13,760
their eyes. You know that door. You

492
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:16,480
closed your own years ago. You wonder if

493
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:19,280
you did them a kindness. You decide not

494
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:22,080
to ask the question. Some of these men

495
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:24,400
will live. Most of them will die out on

496
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:27,039
the sand. You learn to harden yourself

497
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:29,600
against caring too much. It is a lesson

498
00:21:27,039 --> 00:21:31,679
you only ever halflearn.

499
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:34,880
One boy reminds you painfully of your

500
00:21:31,679 --> 00:21:36,720
son. He is the right age for it now. He

501
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:39,679
came from a region close to your old

502
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:42,240
home. For one foolish moment, you let

503
00:21:39,679 --> 00:21:45,039
yourself wonder. Then you stop because

504
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:47,120
the wondering cuts too deep. You drive

505
00:21:45,039 --> 00:21:50,000
him harder than the others. You want him

506
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:52,159
to survive more than anything. He fights

507
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:54,480
his first match and he does not survive

508
00:21:52,159 --> 00:21:56,960
it. You watch the whole thing from the

509
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:59,919
mouth of the tunnel. You do not weep

510
00:21:56,960 --> 00:22:04,640
this time. You have no tears left to

511
00:21:59,919 --> 00:22:06,960
give the sand. Level nine, the Lenista.

512
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:09,200
The years pass and you save every wage

513
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:11,840
you earn. You build careful connections

514
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:14,159
among powerful men. Senators remember

515
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:16,880
your name from the arena. When the old

516
00:22:14,159 --> 00:22:19,440
Lenista finally dies, his school has no

517
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:22,400
master. You gather your savings and

518
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:25,360
favors and buy it. You are 40 years old

519
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:27,840
now, a captive in chains now owns the

520
00:22:25,360 --> 00:22:30,720
gates that once trapped him. It is the

521
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:33,360
strangest victory of your entire life.

522
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:36,159
You are a Lenista now, a master of

523
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:38,799
gladiators. The Romans hold the Lenista

524
00:22:36,159 --> 00:22:41,039
in deep contempt. They use his fighters

525
00:22:38,799 --> 00:22:43,200
for glory and spit on the man who sells

526
00:22:41,039 --> 00:22:45,600
them. You do not care what they think of

527
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:48,080
you anymore. You have been spat upon

528
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:51,039
your whole life. You run the business

529
00:22:48,080 --> 00:22:53,039
with cold and steady eyes. You buy men

530
00:22:51,039 --> 00:22:56,080
at the same market where you were once

531
00:22:53,039 --> 00:22:58,480
sold. You check their teeth. You squeeze

532
00:22:56,080 --> 00:23:00,960
their arms. You make them walk in a

533
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:03,520
circle. You hate that your hands now do

534
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:06,559
these things. You do them anyway because

535
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:09,200
the school must eat. You bargain with

536
00:23:06,559 --> 00:23:11,280
editors and magistrates over prices. You

537
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:13,840
rent your men out for festivals and rich

538
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:16,799
men's funerals. You decide which of them

539
00:23:13,840 --> 00:23:19,039
fight and which are likely to die. The

540
00:23:16,799 --> 00:23:22,080
power that once ruled your every breath

541
00:23:19,039 --> 00:23:24,159
now rests in your hands. You are gentler

542
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:26,559
than the man who once owned you. You

543
00:23:24,159 --> 00:23:29,840
feed your men well. You free the ones

544
00:23:26,559 --> 00:23:32,480
who truly earn their freedom. One day a

545
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:34,720
young Thrian wins his crown. You stand

546
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:37,919
before the crowd. You hand him the

547
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:41,200
wooden sword. He weeps on the sand. He

548
00:23:37,919 --> 00:23:43,919
weeps exactly as you once wept. For a

549
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:46,320
moment, you see your whole life in him.

550
00:23:43,919 --> 00:23:49,039
You free him. You give him coins to

551
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:52,000
start again. You tell him not to come

552
00:23:49,039 --> 00:23:55,200
back here. You know he probably will.

553
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:57,840
They almost always do. The sand keeps

554
00:23:55,200 --> 00:24:00,480
its sons. You watch him walk through the

555
00:23:57,840 --> 00:24:02,799
gates. You envy him with your whole

556
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:05,200
heart. Then you turn back to the

557
00:24:02,799 --> 00:24:07,679
business of blood. But you are still a

558
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:10,880
part of the great machine. The machine

559
00:24:07,679 --> 00:24:12,880
runs on captured men and roaring crowds.

560
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:15,679
You profit from the cruelty that nearly

561
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:18,159
destroyed you. Some nights you sit alone

562
00:24:15,679 --> 00:24:20,640
in the empty yard. You stare at the pale

563
00:24:18,159 --> 00:24:22,880
sand in the moonlight. You wonder how

564
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:27,679
many men have died on it because of your

565
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:30,799
hand. Level 10. the shade. You are old

566
00:24:27,679 --> 00:24:33,600
now. You are past 50, an age no

567
00:24:30,799 --> 00:24:35,919
gladiator was ever meant to reach. Your

568
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:38,480
body is a map of every fight you ever

569
00:24:35,919 --> 00:24:41,200
survived, and the old scars ache through

570
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:43,360
the cold nights. The school you built

571
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:45,919
made you wealthy, respected by the same

572
00:24:43,360 --> 00:24:48,000
men who once paid to watch you bleed.

573
00:24:45,919 --> 00:24:50,720
You sold it years ago when your hands

574
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:53,279
grew too slow to hold the rod. You live

575
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:55,360
in a small villa outside the city. Now

576
00:24:53,279 --> 00:24:58,400
you have a quiet garden, a freed

577
00:24:55,360 --> 00:25:00,640
servant, and a silence you never wanted.

578
00:24:58,400 --> 00:25:03,279
You sit in that garden in the evenings.

579
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:05,039
You watch the light fade over the hills.

580
00:25:03,279 --> 00:25:07,520
You think of all the men who never

581
00:25:05,039 --> 00:25:09,039
reached this quiet. Your friend with the

582
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:12,240
crooked nose should have grown old

583
00:25:09,039 --> 00:25:14,720
beside you. He did not. None of them

584
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:17,279
did. Your name is still spoken in the

585
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:19,679
streets. Boys who were not yet born when

586
00:25:17,279 --> 00:25:22,080
you last fought still carve your stage

587
00:25:19,679 --> 00:25:24,640
name into the plaster. They dream of

588
00:25:22,080 --> 00:25:27,440
glory. They imagine the crowds, the

589
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:30,000
crowns, the hero standing tall over a

590
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:32,240
fallen enemy in the white sun. They do

591
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:34,400
not imagine the cells. They do not

592
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:36,880
imagine the chains, the vomiting in the

593
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:40,159
tunnel, the friend who yielded and was

594
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:42,320
killed anyway. You carry all of it. You

595
00:25:40,159 --> 00:25:45,360
carry the men you killed and the men you

596
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:47,679
trained and then watched die. You carry

597
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:50,720
a wife whose face slipped away from you

598
00:25:47,679 --> 00:25:53,039
decades ago. You carry a son who would

599
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:55,120
be a grown man now somewhere across the

600
00:25:53,039 --> 00:25:57,919
empire who will never know what became

601
00:25:55,120 --> 00:26:00,480
of his father. Or perhaps he died in a

602
00:25:57,919 --> 00:26:02,640
raid at dawn the same way his father was

603
00:26:00,480 --> 00:26:06,000
taken from the world. You will never

604
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:09,039
know which. That not knowing is its own

605
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:12,640
slow wound. You were a captive, a

606
00:26:09,039 --> 00:26:15,440
killer, a champion, a free man, and a

607
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:18,080
master. You were all of these and not

608
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:20,320
one of them was ever your choice. The

609
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:22,640
choice was made for you the morning the

610
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:25,279
soldiers came over the hill. When you

611
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:28,080
die, there will be no monument, no

612
00:26:25,279 --> 00:26:30,799
record, no honest account of the man you

613
00:26:28,080 --> 00:26:33,440
truly were. There will only be a name on

614
00:26:30,799 --> 00:26:36,880
crumbling plaster, fading a little more

615
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:39,840
with every passing year. Somewhere right

616
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:41,600
now, far beyond a great river, soldiers

617
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:44,559
are moving toward a sleeping village at

618
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:47,360
dawn. A young man is waking beside his

619
00:26:44,559 --> 00:26:49,760
wife and his small child. He has never

620
00:26:47,360 --> 00:26:52,320
heard the name of Rome. He has never

621
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:55,120
held a sword. He does not know that men

622
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:56,720
in iron are already coming for him. He

623
00:26:55,120 --> 00:26:59,200
does not know that a chain waits

624
00:26:56,720 --> 00:27:02,559
somewhere with his name upon it. He will

625
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:05,559
learn. They always do. The cycle

626
00:27:02,559 --> 00:27:05,559
continues.

